  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The State of Illinois recorded $8.9B in federal contract obligations, FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 27.7% year over year. Award activity totaled 381,771 actions with an average award size of $23.4K. Federal buying concentrated: the Department of Defense obligated $4.4B, the Department of Energy obligated $1.8B, and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $1.6B. Large vendors captured major shares: UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC received $1B, W S DARLEY & CO received $930M, and MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP received $772M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $1B, and Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers accounted for $1B. FY2026 to date obligations of $8.9B sit below recent fiscal-year peaks of $13.6B in FY22 and $13.4B in FY24. All figures are contract obligations and the current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 compare with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations in FY2026 to date are $8.9B, below the FY22 peak of $13.6B and the FY24 total of $13.4B. Obligations fell 27.7% year over year. Award count remained substantial at 381,771 with an average award size of $23.4K, indicating many small awards despite the lower total. FY2026 totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominate Illinois federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $4.4B, followed by the Department of Energy with $1.8B and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $1.6B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences and Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers each accounted for $1B in obligations. Major vendors include UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC at $1B and W S DARLEY & CO at $930M. Industry and vendor concentration shows a mix of research, medical supplies, and manufacturing activity."
      }
    ]
  },
